  "problem": "There are $121$ boys in Eastwood High School. The ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls is $3:5.$ By rounding the number of boys to the nearest ten, approximate the number of girls in Eastwood High School.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of boys:\n\n$$\n121⟶120\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the number of boys and the denominator represents the number of girls.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $120$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $40$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 40}{5\\times 40}=\\frac{120}{200}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $200$ girls in Eastwood High School.",
